  "name": "Prisoner Box Squat with Overhead Reach",
  "definition": "A bodyweight box squat and seated overhead reach shown in the Boxing Science video. Start standing with hands interlocked behind the head, sit back onto a bench, release the hands and reach both arms up in a wide V while seated, return the hands behind the head, then stand. The bench supports the seated reach. This is one rep-counted sequence, with no external load or measured mobility outcome. The seated reach distinguishes it from the active unsupported bodyweight squat.",
