      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Stand in front of a bench with feet comfortably wide. Interlock both hands behind the head and keep the elbows open.",
        "movement": "Sit back onto the bench with the knees tracking out over the feet. While seated, release the hands and reach both arms up in a wide V.",
        "endpoint": "Reach overhead while the pelvis is supported on the bench and the trunk stays controlled.",
        "returnPhase": "Bring the hands behind the head while seated, then press through both feet to stand upright.",
        "controlledJoints": "Keep the feet planted, avoid letting the knees cave inward, and raise the arms without flaring the rib cage.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Use the bench for a brief seated position; keep the trunk braced during the reach and rise.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": [
          "Keeping the hands behind the head throughout omits the defining overhead reach.",
          "Reaching overhead while standing changes the reviewed seated phase.",
